id: pm-slack-standup-packed-timing
title: Investigate packed npm and Bun acceptance exceeding the unchanged local timeout under shared load
description: "Direct source npm release validation on the toolchain bump ran 287 tests: 285 passed, and the two real packed acceptance matrices exceeded their existing 290000 ms subprocess timeout. The matrices cover npm-current, bun-current, npm-minimum, bun-minimum and npm-global-current. Earlier branch CI completed the same matrices and reached only the separate changelog drift. Preserve timeout and coverage thresholds; distinguish host contention or install cost from package regressions. Validation evidence is on pm-slack-standup-jnje."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-26T18:53:49.669Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-31T02:33:16.752Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Explain and reproduce the instrumented packed-install timing discrepancy; retain the 290000 ms subprocess timeout and every coverage threshold; record standalone and full npm/Bun receipts
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T19:08:31.471Z",codex-agent,"Standalone acceptance completed all five scenarios with matching SDK identities, rendered fixture counts and no missing fixture data. Full npm and Bun gates each passed 285/287 tests and timed out only their two instrumented real-install matrices. This separates functional acceptance from the unchanged 290000 ms budget; investigate instrumentation, fresh per-scenario caches and shared scheduling without lowering coverage or increasing that timeout."
  "2026-10-31T00:59:00.361Z",codex-agent,"Cursor-window delivery validation repeats the existing instrumented limit: complete isolated npm release check ran 350 tests, 348 passed, and only both real-install matrices exceeded 290000 ms. Runtime modules measured 100% in all four dimensions; acceptance-script paths left unexecuted by timeout reduced global coverage to 96.17% lines/statements, 99.88% branches, 97.59% functions. No timeout or coverage threshold was changed. Current-source Node/Bun standalone receipts and exact-head CI will be linked from pm-slack-standup-kovw."
  "2026-10-31T01:23:33.985Z",codex-agent,"Bun full release validation also completed 348/350 tests, failing only the same two 290000 ms matrix timeouts. Its runtime-module coverage and overall authored-source percentages match the npm receipt. Preserve this as timing evidence; it is not a passing release gate. Final-source standalone fresh-pack receipts and CI are pending on pm-slack-standup-kovw."
  "2026-10-31T01:48:44.387Z",codex-agent,"Final-source standalone acceptance completed every scenario: 6/6 under Node and 6/6 under Bun, with byte-identical fresh artifacts. This distinguishes functional packed acceptance from both complete local release gates (348/350 each; two 290-second instrumented timeouts each). Runtime coverage is 100% in every dimension; the overall gate remains failed at unchanged thresholds. Current evidence and the PR check board are tracked by pm-slack-standup-kovw."
  "2026-10-31T01:52:14.074Z",codex-agent,"Related implementation and final-source evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/pull/175 . This follow-up remains open: standalone Node/Bun packed scenarios pass 6/6 each, but both complete local release gates still hit the two unchanged instrumented 290-second limits. The PR check board will carry exact-head CI results; this comment does not claim the timing issue is fixed."
  "2026-10-31T02:18:44.040Z",codex-agent,"The Node 22 failure reproduced in CI at 349/350 tests (one matrix timed out; the other completed in 264544 ms). The driver now shares only integrity-checked package download caches within one temporary run, disables redundant fixture audit/funding work, and removes V8 counter output only from installed-consumer subprocesses outside the canonical source inventory. Trackers, installs and configuration remain separate. The canonical acceptance driver and source helper subprocesses retain profiling. All assertions, six scenarios, two launcher modes, worker cap, 290-second limit and 100% source thresholds remain unchanged. Focused driver contracts pass 12/12."
  "2026-10-31T02:33:13.979Z",codex-agent,"Implemented per-run download caching and installed-consumer counter isolation without changing any matrix assertion, scenario, timeout, worker limit, source inventory or threshold. Focused contracts pass 12/12; the counter-isolation behavioral revert fails and restores 1/1. Canonical driver/source-helper profiling stays enabled. Replacement-head CI will determine whether the original Node 22 timeout is resolved; no success is presumed."
